title: EMR Connect › Manage › Open the Manage drawer
route: /emr
intro: One system's details in a right-hand drawer: connection facts, what the agents may read, whether it is read only or read and write back (in words), and a Disconnect or Reconnect button. A system that is not Connected says here that New Case cannot pull a chart from it. The Write back switch and the field mappings are not here: the switch is on the system's row, the mappings are in 'Advanced'.
dir: TD
also: Drawer buttons that the demo does not have: pause, edit, rename, delete, rotate sign-in. The only way to stop a system is Disconnect, and a system is never removed. Escape closes one layer at a time, so a pop-up on top of the drawer closes first. The header button 'Manage mapping' no longer exists: the mappings sit in 'Advanced'.
---
start s1 "Click 'Manage' on a row"
overlay o1 "Drawer: {system name}\n'{kind} · {what it holds}'\nStatus pill on the right, X at the top"

group gDet "Card: Connection details"
  process d1 "Type, Connected since, Contact at the practice\nLast sync: 'N min ago' or 'Not syncing'\nAccess: 'Secure, read-only connection'"
  toast d2 "Only when it is not Connected\nThe issue text, for example the expired sign-in, then 'New Case cannot pull a chart from it until it is connected.'"
endgroup

group gPerm "Card: Permissions"
  process r1 "Read chips depend on the kind\nClinical record: Assessments, Progress notes, Labs, Medications, Insurance card\nBilling system: Claims, Remittances, Payment dates\nPractice management: Schedules, Admissions, Insurance card\nLab results: Lab orders, Lab results"
  process w1 "'Read and write back' or 'Read only', with one sentence\n'Change it with the Write back switch on the system's row. Field mappings are under Advanced on the page.'\nNo switch in the drawer"
endgroup

process n1 "The Dashboard reads the switches on the rows\nIt offers the approval write-back box only while at least one Connected system has the switch on"
goto g3 "Continues in: EMR Connect › Connected systems › Read only or read and write back"

decision bq "Is the system Disconnected?"
click b1 "Click 'Disconnect'\nRed outline button"
click b2 "Click 'Reconnect'\nGreen button"
click cx "Click the X, press Escape, or click the dimmed area\nA pop-up on top closes first"
end e1 "Drawer closes\nBack on the page"
goto g2 "Continues in: EMR Connect › Manage › Disconnect and reconnect"
goto g4 "Continues in: EMR Connect › Manage › Reconnect a system"
goto g5 "Continues in: EMR Connect › Advanced › Field mappings and the activity log"

s1 --> o1
o1 --> d1 & r1
d1 -.-> d2
r1 --> w1
w1 -.-> n1
w1 -.-> g3
w1 -.-> g5
o1 --> bq
bq -->|No| b1 --> g2
bq -->|Yes| b2 --> g4
o1 -.-> cx --> e1
